# Farmer Order Management Module Implementation Plan

This document outlines the architecture and execution plan for the Farmer Order Management Module. It provides farmers with a comprehensive dashboard to track, accept, pack, and ship orders while maintaining synchronization with the simulated escrow smart contract.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Action Realism vs Simulation:** While the UI will display blockchain validations, the actual backend interactions (like releasing escrow or refunding) will be simulated database updates for now, as real Arbitrum testnet deployment requires live private keys and funded wallets.
> **Order Tracking Real-time Updates:** I will implement standard REST polling for now to avoid setting up a complex WebSocket server architecture in Rust Axum during this sandbox session, ensuring high stability.

## Open Questions
- Do you require Courier Tracking APIs (like Shiprocket or Delhivery) to be actually integrated, or is a simple input form for "Tracking Number" sufficient for this phase?

